<p>
<u>28-AUG-2005 10:45 PM (BKK Time)</u><br>
I'd like to start off today with some facts about Thailand that I have come across or observed.  Did you know that:
<li>There are 6 million people in Thailand and 4 million people that commute to the city?<br>
<li>There are 400 temples in BKK, 500 in Ayutthaya.<br>
<li>The current King, King Rama IX has been on the throne for 60 years.<br>
<li>The floating market has been going for over 100 years.<br>
<li>All young men must be Buddhist monks for 3 months before they reach the age of 21.  During those 3 months, the government pays for you to become a monk.<br>
<li>95% of Thais are Buddhist.<br>
<li>There are pics of King Rama IX and the Queen or both alongside the highways and on the buildings and signs in the city.<br>
<li>Street vendors sell bootleg DVDs, porn, lingerie, and dildos from carts on the sidewalk<br>
<li>There are lots of old white men with young single beautiful Thai girls.<br>
<p>
This morning Mr. Duty had decided to go into town with us.  We didn't have much time at all because I forgot to setup my alarm clock, so M and I had to get ready fast as the tour left at 6:45 AM instead of the normal 8:45 AM.  Therefore, we didn't have time for breakfast.
<p>
We got to the hotel with 15 min to spare but the coffee shop below didn't open until 7 AM.  The tour guide was late but not late enough as she got there before the coffee shop could open.
<p>
We weren't fortunate this time to have the tour bus to ourselves.  It was completely packed.  I noticed we had the multinational tour bus.  I had counted 5 different languages being spoken at once - Thai, Hindi, Italian, English, and Filipino.  Shows you how much of a tourist attraction Thailand really is.  
<p>
Our first stop was a coconut farm.  We were shown how a coconut flower looks like and how it produced a sap-like substanced that was cooked and filtered until it became solidified brown sugar.  As for the rest of the coconut, you can drink the coconut milk and eat the fleshy part.  And there is quite nothing like eaching a fresh coconut so M and I had to try one.
<p>
