<p>
Afterwards, we went to a handicraft woodcarving shop where furniture is hand-carved with intricate designs and assembled.  I noticed several of the buyers were from the US.  The work is quite amazing as they draw 2D drawings on paper, tape them to the wood and carve them right into the wood making it 3D.  Prices averaged about $10K USD but it is a one of a kind custom made furniture.  Let's just say that for the amount of time and talent put on just one section of furniture, $10K is a bargain.
<p>
